@@ -47,5 +47,5 @@
       <p>Daily email and mobile push reminders are disabled by default and require separate explicit choices. You control the days, local time and timezone, and can disable either channel in Account settings. Email reminders go only to the verified email on your Pack One account, and include unsubscribe and management links. Device notifications require an additional device permission and use a device-specific push token. Granting email consent does not grant push consent.</p>
       <p>To deliver reminders, Pack One stores your schedule, channel-specific consent times, a minimal change history, device registrations with protected push tokens, delivery attempts and provider receipt states. Resend receives the verified email and email contents for subscribed messages; Expo and device push providers handle native notification tokens and message content. A provider accepting an email or push does not guarantee its appearance or delivery. Bounce and complaint events can disable email reminders.</p>
-      <p>Pack One removes reminder preferences, send records, and device registrations when your account is deleted. Changing accounts or signing out revokes the corresponding device registration. Unsubscribing from email does not affect push. Pack One does not sell reminder destinations or publicly report individual reminder activity.</p>
+      <p>Pack One removes reminder preferences, send records, and device registrations when your account is deleted. Delivery records are otherwise kept for up to 90 days, change history for up to 365 days, and revoked device registrations for up to 30 days; cleanup runs with the reminder scheduler. Bounce and complaint suppression fingerprints remain until account deletion to honor delivery restrictions. Changing accounts or signing out revokes the corresponding device registration. Unsubscribing from email does not affect push. A message already handed to an email or device provider cannot be recalled. Pack One does not sell reminder destinations or publicly report individual reminder activity.</p>
       <h2>Gameplay, analytics, and decision reports</h2>
       <p>Pack One stores gameplay inputs and results needed to score runs, preserve progress, show history, support Daily leaderboards, and operate account features. Pack One also records product events such as page views, game starts, reveals, challenge opens and completions, shares, and outbound commerce clicks so it can understand whether the product works and where players stop in the experience.</p>
